From ce08eef0458585340212b70c211a5dd948f16af3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Wed, 8 Apr 2026 08:52:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/26] fix(hooks): include gt costs record in polecat Stop
 hook
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The claude-settings doctor check requires `costs record` to appear
in every Stop hook (claude_settings_check.go:568), but the polecat
override in DefaultOverrides() replaced the default Stop hook
(`gt costs record &`) with only `gt tap polecat-stop-check`.

Result: gt doctor reported 19 polecat settings.json files as "stale
— missing Stop hook" on every run, and `gt doctor --fix` couldn't
self-heal because it regenerated the same broken template.

Fix: add `gt costs record &` as a second hook entry under the
polecat Stop override so both the idle-polecat check and cost
recording run on session stop.
---
 internal/hooks/config.go | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/internal/hooks/config.go b/internal/hooks/config.go
index fbf5ef61..95d4c6f1 100644
--- a/internal/hooks/config.go
+++ b/internal/hooks/config.go
@@ -213,6 +213,8 @@ func DefaultOverrides() map[string]*HooksConfig {
 		// forget to call gt done before the session ends. The polecat-stop-check
 		// command is idempotent — it checks heartbeat state and branch commits
 		// before deciding whether to run gt done.
+		// Also records costs (keeps claude-settings doctor check happy, which
+		// expects `costs record` in every Stop hook).
 		"polecats": {
 			Stop: []HookEntry{
 				{
@@ -222,6 +224,10 @@ func DefaultOverrides() map[string]*HooksConfig {
 							Type:    "command",
 							Command: hookChain(pathSetup, "gt tap polecat-stop-check"),
 						},
+						{
+							Type:    "command",
+							Command: hookChain(pathSetup, "gt costs record &"),
+						},
 					},
 				},
 			},
-- 
